  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR keeps the released 0.26.0 guide fixes on main.\nThe first commit comes from #3771 without a conflict.\nThe PR changes only `site/`.\n\n1. `guide/check-and-post/posting.md` lists all 26 supplied post scripts, their controls, and all 50 machine files. It explains native Agie job limits.\n2. `guide/operations/operations-2d.md` documents Do not touch on Face, Trace, and Engrave. It preserves the existing 2D Adaptive guidance. `operations-3d.md` adds 3D Finish guidance.\n3. `guide/set-up/setups.md` explains typed outline text through MCP and app profile placement. It states the released dialog and generation limits.\n4. `guide/operations/operations-2d.md` warns about Inside and Outside ramps and lifts on 2D Offset. It links #3741 and #3744 through #3748.\n5. `guide/reference/migrating.md` explains format 78, part-off regeneration, and the unitless STEP question. It links the existing unit rules.\n\nThe review fix brings the requested site files from #3768 onto this branch:\n\n- Add the missing Multi-Axis Deburr and Waterjet Profile icons. Keep their site bytes equal to the app assets.\n- Add both operation references and their path diagrams. Link the Waterjet page from the operation index and machine guide.\n- Add the `onJetOff()` and `onJetOn()` hook signatures.\n- Add the `lineEnding`, `linearizeArcs`, and `uprightReturn` manifest rows.\n- Extend the existing inventory pins for these names.\n\nRelease PR #3771 targets `site/v0.26.0`. The maintainer deploys that PR with the `release.yml` `site_only` dispatch.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe guide omitted shipped features and release-specific limitations.\nFacts come from the 0.26.0 tree, including `assets/posts/`, `assets/machines/`, and `crates/`.\nDecisions and the first hunk review are recorded on #3769 because this branch permits only site files.\nThe latest review also found missing reference entries and assets that made the complete site suite fail.\nThose fixes now exist on this PR head.\n\n## Tests\n\nFinal head: `274cbb11aad5ffb318946d26171aa7f1f25bc7d6`.\nCurrent base: upstream/main `79d47c28229aaad15a564c82d0214debae0473ef`.\nThe quick gate compares against merge base `7868d3786`.\n\n- `ZOLA=/tmp/review-3772-tools/zola python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests -v`: passed; 99 tests, no failures (3.906 seconds).\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=1 CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=1 cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: passed on the final head; 0 selected steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (site-only diff).\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo test -j 6 -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog -- --test-threads=6`: passed on the final head; 39 passed, 0 failed, 4 ignored (26.20 seconds).\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- The site tests use Zola 0.23.6 and Node v22.22.1.\n\nReview pins:\n\n| Finding | Test |\n|---|---|\n| Missing site icons and inventory | `GuideIcons.test_component_static_icons_and_license_match_app` |\n| Missing operation references and pictures | `OperationReferencePictures.test_every_operation_has_section_and_picture` |\n| Missing jet hook signatures | `PostProcessorReference.test_engine_hooks_have_reference_entries` |\n| Missing manifest rows | `PostProcessorReference.test_manifest_properties_have_reference_rows` |\n\nMutation proof: nine separate mutations failed with assertion failures, without test errors. Each restored fix passed its pin. The mutations removed each icon, each operation heading, each jet hook signature, and each manifest row separately.\nEach mutation keeps the test changes and removes only the corresponding fix.\n\nThe first commit also has five pins in `test_release_026_gaps.Release026Gaps`:\n\n- `test_post_inventory_names_each_shipped_script_and_control`\n- `test_do_not_touch_is_documented_on_each_added_operation`\n- `test_outline_text_explains_creation_and_profile_use`\n- `test_offset_warns_about_released_inside_outside_paths`\n- `test_upgrade_notes_cover_format_regeneration_and_unit_question`\n\nThe first author run showed all five fail before the fix.\nSix mutations restored the old inventory, 2D protection, Offset warning, Finish protection, outline page, and upgrade page.\nEach mutation failed its pins. Each restored fix passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The example catalog suite passed. No recorded program changed: `git diff --name-only upstream/main...HEAD -- '*.nc' '*.cl' 'examples/catalog/**'` is empty. The example catalog result is listed above.\nNo recorded programs or catalog files change in this PR.\nNo golden suite is reached by these site files.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nHeavy lanes: not applicable. The diff changes site content, static assets, and Python tests only.\nIt changes no motion, simulation, post implementation, geometry, or app operation code.\nClippy: not applicable. No Rust crate is touched.\nNo controller acceptance or interactive app test ran.\nNo app UI code changes, so app before/after screenshots are not applicable.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #3766 changes V-Carve. PR #3103 changes Bore.\nEach touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nThis round copies eight content and asset files from #3768 and extends three existing test files.\nIt does not import #3768's product history or decision file.\nThe PR remains a draft for an independent review.\n\nChangelog: none (docs only)\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3769\n",
